SHA256 written on the builtin type Word32.T (this fork; see
LLVM-IR-backend-docs/fixed-width-integer-types-plan.md, Phase 4),
with plain +, the Word32 rotates and shifts, and no masking.  Main
checks its digests against libm3's SHA256 (which masks INTEGERs) and
against the published values of the standard test vectors, including
the lengths at which the padding needs a second block.  Every line
of output should be the same with every backend and at every
optimization level.
